WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
A figure in black holds
up a mask, labelled mad.

2
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:09.310
He has warned his friends he may choose
"To put an antic disposition on".

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.920
He puts the mask on and
walks into a crowded court.

4
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.280
Alone again, he takes it off.

5
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.930
But the scenes speed up:
with Ophelia, with Polonius,

6
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.190
with his mother.

7
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.660
In each one, is the mask on, or off?

8
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.970
Hamlet says he'll fake madness.

9
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.350
So does he stay in control of it?

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.470
In this mission, you'll
map who sees which Hamlet,

11
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.050
scene by scene.

12
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.380
You'll weigh the question
readers keep asking:

13
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.180
why does he delay?

14
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.370
And you'll find performances
everywhere in the play.

15
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.140
Your mission: decide whether
Hamlet stays in control.
